# Interpreter selection correction after actual Windows start failure

The approved driver did not start: Windows rejected direct execution of the installed WindowsApps python.exe with Access is denied. The actual tool result is retained in campaign-preparation-driver/actual-start-01-failed-before-python.json. Both selected fresh roots were subsequently observed absent. No driver byte ran, so no campaign preparation or source import occurred.

Actual metadata obtained through the existing working Python launcher is retained in preparation-tool-files-launcher-resolution.json (SHA256 11caf55b22bcdf85fefe9f8b599ffa63c97013f636ad2b4f15bf8e24164312dc). It identifies C:/WINDOWS/py.EXE, SHA256 7a2dad0ccad20e9ddf1217aa1ca3af9ae12207b4990d17d6a5192c28bba3ea36, and the native Windows app alias returned in sys.executable. The installed binary under sys.base_prefix still matches the previously selected physical binary SHA256 ad169f4cb4bfb78c7a5c030a4529c19d6643276778e33994c93e145b6191c3ec. The alias is a zero-byte APPEXECLINK reparse entry and cannot be hashed as executable content; do not claim its bytes equal those of the installed binary.

Principal decision: use the exact observed launcher with -3.13 -B for actual preparation and eventual approved launch. Before project imports or destination writes, authenticate the launcher file hash, exact native sys.executable and sys._base_executable alias paths, exact sys.base_prefix, Python version, and readable installed binary hash. Record the native alias and installed binary separately. Keep Git/Docker paths and hashes unchanged. Do not change or substitute sys.executable, os.environ, native artifact/config/owner identities, or renderer behavior. This is a genuine installed-interpreter selection correction, not an operational capability substitute.

This supersedes only the direct-physical-executable requirement in native-launch-envelope-notes.md, the driver review brief, and the concrete review brief. The native renderer must still emit the unchanged actual sys.executable alias followed by -B -m core.pit_optimizer_v5.cli and exact policy-pinned campaign arguments. The saved eventual launch uses the exact launcher to start the same actual interpreter, then the existing awake/credential helpers forward those native campaign arguments (starting at native argv index4) into the canonical CLI. No alias file hash or direct-start success is asserted.

The driver needs a narrow source correction and independent review before retrying actual preparation. All earlier source, readiness, graph, artifact, budget and no-paid-execution gates remain unchanged. There was no automatic approval-review rejection and no request for elevation. A fresh paid-run grant is still required only after the actual package and launch are independently reviewed.
